  "lineage": "Jamaican ska (1959-1965, fast-tempo guitar-upbeat horn-section-foregrounded dance music) and its slower-tempo derivation rocksteady (1965-1968) — codified at Studio One, Treasure Isle, and Federal through the Skatalites (Tommy McCook, Don Drummond, Roland Alphonso, Lloyd Knibb, the ska house band), Prince Buster, Toots and the Maytals, the Wailers (early-period), Alton Ellis (Get Ready Rocksteady), Ken Boothe, the Heptones; preceded reggae and remains foundational to the broader Jamaican popular music lineage",
